# Library-tree overrides layered on the root .clang-tidy (which is symlinked
# into the pico-tooling submodule and shared across the pico-* repos).
#
# Diagnostics raised inside a header are governed by the configuration of the
# translation unit that includes it, not by the config next to the header. So
# an exemption pico-sh2 carries for its own tree has to be restated here for its
# headers to be quiet when this repo's sources include them. Every entry below
# is one that actually fires: a rule disabled where it reports nothing is silent
# coverage loss for every file added later, not an exemption.
InheritParentConfig: true

Checks: >
  -readability-magic-numbers

# readability-magic-numbers: the numbers are the datasheet's and the protocol
# manuals'. Pin assignments, register values, wire lengths, field offsets and Q
# points are each cited to the document and section that defines them; naming
# every one would add a layer between the code and the document it has to be
# checked against. Reaches pico-sh2's transcribed wire format through the
# headers this tree includes.
